Yes — it's a one-liner in the Electron main process. Currently the `will-navigate` / `new-window` hooks in [app.ts:194-198](apps/electron-backend/src/app/app.ts:194) are commented out, so `target="_blank"` opens a blank Electron child window instead of the system browser.

The idiomatic fix is `webContents.setWindowOpenHandler` with `shell.openExternal` — no changes needed in the Angular code, the existing anchors keep working:

```ts
App.mainWindow.webContents.setWindowOpenHandler(({ url }) => {
    if (/^https?:\/\//.test(url)) {
        shell.openExternal(url);
    }
    return { action: 'deny' };
});
```

Drop it into [initMainWindow](apps/electron-backend/src/app/app.ts:190) near the other `webContents` hooks. This covers every `target="_blank"` link app-wide (About, EPG note, future links) and PWA mode is unaffected — the browser already opens new tabs normally.

Want me to add it?

